    <h2>Hi, I am Reem</h2>
    <div class="split">
    <div>
      <!-- The summary that search engines and assistants lift to answer "who is Reem
           Glasco". Keep every fact in it: name, credential, city, the year, the
           certifications and both fees. -->
      <div class="answer">
        <p>I am Reem Glasco, LPC-S, in Austin, Texas. I have held Texas supervisor status since
        2009 and I am an EMDRIA Approved Consultant, a NARM therapist and a Somatic Experiencing
        Practitioner. My clinical center is IFS-informed EMDR: processing that consults the
        protective parts of a person instead of overriding them. Somatic Experiencing sets the
        pace and NARM tracks the patterns underneath, and that is the same lens whether you are
        my supervisee or my client. Supervision and EMDR consultation run online statewide, and
        some of the work happens on a trail or with horses rather than on a screen.</p>
      </div>
      <p>Supervision here is clinical work rather than paperwork. The associates I work best
      with want more than signed hours: they want to understand what is happening in the room,
      including what is happening in their own nervous system while a client is falling apart
      in front of them.</p>
      <p>I expect you to show up prepared, be honest, and tell me when something goes wrong.
      In return you get help building a practice, not just a log.</p>
