<section class="band band--night" id="therapists">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>The four ways I work with therapists</h2>
    <p class="intro-wide">Supervision, consultation, ethics hours and retreats are different
    things, and most therapists arrive wanting one of them in particular. All of it runs online
    across Texas, apart from the parts that deliberately happen on a trail or with horses.</p>
    <div class="pathways">
      <a href="/for-therapists/lpc-supervision/">
        <h3>LPC supervision</h3>
        <p>Your 3,000 hours, supervised online anywhere in Texas. Four hours a month,
          trauma-informed, with EMDR consultation included while you are here. If you are an
          associate working toward licensure, start here.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/for-therapists/emdr-consultation/">
        <h3>EMDR consultation</h3>
        <p>Hours toward certification with an EMDRIA Approved Consultant. Online, focused on
        IFS-informed EMDR for phases one and two.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/for-therapists/ethics-ceus/">
        <h3>Ethics CEUs</h3>
        <p>The six ethics hours Texas asks for each renewal period, on secondary trauma. One
        online, or two in person on a trail walk among horses.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/for-therapists/retreats-training/">
        <h3>Retreats and training</h3>
        <p>Mindful trail retreats and equine-assisted training for Texas therapists. For when
        the growth edge is yours rather than a client's.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--sand" id="clients">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>Four ways I work with clients</h2>
    <p class="intro-wide">I see a small number of adults and young adults for developmental
    trauma, C-PTSD, anxiety, panic and depression. When my schedule is full, the practice's
    <a href="/therapy/associates/">LPC Associates</a> have openings, including at sliding-scale
    fees.</p>
    <div class="pathways">
      <a href="/approach/ifs-informed-emdr/">
        <h3>IFS-informed EMDR</h3>
        <p>Internal agreement from the protective parts first, then processing.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/somatic-experiencing/">
        <h3>Somatic Experiencing</h3>
        <p>The pace your nervous system can actually hold, built rather than tested.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/narm/">
        <h3>NARM</h3>
        <p>The pattern underneath, and where it was learned.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/therapy/equine/">
        <h3>Equine-assisted therapy</h3>
        <p>What the body does around a horse that notices everything.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="intro-wide">These four interlock rather than alternate, and the room is optional.
    <a href="/therapy/walk-and-talk/">Walk and talk therapy</a> happens on a trail in central
    Texas, and equine sessions run with the horses near Dripping Springs.
    <a href="/therapy/">Learn more about therapy at Finding Balance</a>, including fees, formats
    and what a first session looks like.</p>
  </div>
